5 704 M
(What does \342\\200\\234present truth\342\\200\\235 or \342\\200\\234truth for this time\342\\200\\235 mean?) s
5 678 M
(Present truth is not a different gospel. It is the truth God's people especially need for the time ) s
5 665 M
(they are living in.) s
5 639 M
(Ask first what phase of God's work is at the center in a given period. Ellen White's own point is ) s
5 626 M
(that there are many precious truths in the Word of God, but present truth is what the flock ) s
5 613 M
(needs now. So the question is not whether other doctrines are true. The question is which truths ) s
5 600 M
(are especially urgent for the hour God's people are living in.) s
5 574 M
(Walk through redemptive history. When Christ was born, present truth was that the Messiah ) s
5 561 M
(had come. When John the Baptist announced Christ's ministry, that was present truth for that ) s
5 548 M
(hour. At Pentecost, present truth centered on Christ entering His priestly work. In 1844, present ) s
5 535 M
(truth centered on the cleansing of the sanctuary. Each stage had truth for that time because each ) s
5 522 M
(stage highlighted what Christ was then doing.) s
5 496 M
(So for the present time, the governing center is what Jesus is doing now in the heavenly ) s
5 483 M
(sanctuary, especially in the most holy place. That is why the sanctuary in connection with the ) s
5 470 M
(2300 days, the commandments of God, the faith of Jesus, the Sabbath, the state of the dead, and ) s
5 457 M
(the judgment are treated as present truth. These truths explain the Advent movement, show ) s
5 444 M
(where God's people stand, steady the doubting, and give certainty about what lies ahead.) s
5 418 M
(That does not make the rest of Scripture unimportant. All truth is precious. But the burden of ) s
5 405 M
(the message must stay on the truths the flock needs now, not on side subjects that pull attention ) s
5 392 M
(away from what unites God's people and sanctifies the soul.) s
5 366 M
(Will both immature and mature believers be sealed before probation closes?) s
5 340 M
(Yes, but the source does not answer that by opening a sealing passage and walking through it ) s
5 327 M
(verse by verse. It answers it from the end-time situation they are assuming.) s
5 301 M
(Start with that setting. God will still call people out of Babylon near the end, and many of them ) s
5 288 M
(will not have had long years to mature inside the church before the close of probation. That is ) s
5 275 M
(why 11th-hour workers matter here. Some people will come in late.) s
5 249 M
(But late is not the same thing as shallow. Their point is that these believers may be latecomers in ) s
5 236 M
(time and still grow faithfully with the light they receive. By God's grace they can accept the ) s
5 223 M
(Sabbath truth, submit to God's authority, and reject a counterfeit system of worship.) s
5 197 M
(That is where the final test comes in. The issue is loyalty, not seniority. The world will be ) s
5 184 M
(pressed to choose between God's authority and a counterfeit Christianity enforcing Sunday in ) s
5 171 M
(place of the Sabbath. On that logic, those who are sealed are not measured mainly by how many ) s
5 158 M
(years they have been in the church, but by whether they have surrendered and obeyed what ) s
5 145 M
(Christ has shown them.) s
5 119 M
(So there will be 11th-hour workers, and their growth can be accelerated under the stress of the ) s
5 106 M
(final crisis and the power of the loud cry. Some who come in late may grow faster than people ) s
5 93 M
(who have been in the church a long time. Maturity, as they are using the idea here, is not ) s
5 80 M
(measured by calendar time but by the depth of surrender and obedience to known truth.) s
5 54 M
(What does 1 Timothy 5:22 mean about not sharing in the sins of others?) s
5 28 M
(The verse is about ordaining church leaders, not about praying for others.) s
5 2 M
(Read it in context. From 1 Timothy 5:17 onward, Paul is giving Timothy instructions on elders ) s
_R
S
