5 704 M
(this your voice, my son David? And Saul lifted up his voice, and wept. And he said to David, ) s
5 691 M
(You are more righteous than I: for you have rewarded me good, whereas I have rewarded you ) s
5 678 M
(evil." That is what coals of fire on the head looks like. The enemy is convicted by the kindness.) s
5 652 M
(Paul takes the same proverb into the New Testament in Romans 12:19-20. "Beloved, avenge not ) s
5 639 M
(yourselves, but rather give place unto wrath: for it is written, Vengeance is mine; I will repay, ) s
5 626 M
(says the Lord. Therefore if your enemy hungers, feed him; if he thirsts, give him drink: for in so ) s
5 613 M
(doing you shall heap coals of fire on his head." Whatever else it means, Paul is plainly using it ) s
5 600 M
(to forbid personal revenge. Leave vengeance to God, and go on doing good.) s
5 574 M
(Some have taken the image a step further and read the fire as a symbol of the Holy Spirit ) s
5 561 M
(bringing conviction, so that kindness wins a friend. That is offered as an interpretation, not as ) s
5 548 M
(what the text itself says in so many words. What the text does say is plain enough: do not take ) s
5 535 M
(revenge, meet the need of the one who opposes you, and trust God to reward it. In its wider ) s
5 522 M
(context that is what Micah 6:8 calls for \342\\200\\224 do justly, love mercy, walk humbly with God ) s
5 509 M
(\342\\200\\224 even, and especially, under opposition.) s
5 483 M
(What is the mark of the beast according to the Bible, and is it a microchip or biometric system?) s
5 457 M
(The mark of the beast is not a microchip, barcode, biometric scan, or some other tracking ) s
5 444 M
(device. Those things may become mechanisms of control, but they are not the mark itself.) s
5 418 M
(Read Revelation 13 first. The chapter speaks about beasts, worship, authority, and the ) s
5 405 M
(enforcement of allegiance. That is why the first distinction matters so much. Separate the mark ) s
5 392 M
(of the beast from the mechanism used to enforce it. A cashless system, a digital control grid, or ) s
5 379 M
(some other technology could be used to restrict buying and selling, but that would only be the ) s
5 366 M
(tool used to pressure conscience. It would not itself be the mark.) s
5 340 M
(Then identify the powers in Revelation 13. The first beast is identified as the papal power. The ) s
5 327 M
(second beast is identified as the United States, which eventually raises up an image to the beast ) s
5 314 M
(and enforces its demands. So the issue is not mainly economics or technology. The issue is ) s
5 301 M
(worship and whose authority you submit to.) s
5 275 M
(That is where Sunday comes in. The argument is that the papacy itself claims Sunday as the ) s
5 262 M
(sign of its authority, because it claims power to change God's law from Sabbath to Sunday. On ) s
5 249 M
(that reading, Sunday observance right now is not yet the mark of the beast simply because there ) s
5 236 M
(has not yet been a universal legal test compelling worship on that basis. The mark becomes the ) s
5 223 M
(mark in the full prophetic sense when Sunday observance is enforced by law and the world is ) s
5 210 M
(pressed to choose between God's authority and the authority of a rival religious system.) s
5 184 M
(Keep that qualification in view. Not every sincere Sundaykeeper already has the mark of the ) s
5 171 M
(beast. They explicitly say that crisis point has not yet come, that many sincere Christians are ) s
5 158 M
(serving God according to the light they presently have, and that the final test comes when the ) s
5 145 M
(issue is made clear and conscience is forced.) s
5 119 M
(That turns the issue into a Bible-versus-tradition question. If a person says he goes by the Bible ) s
5 106 M
(only, yet keeps Sunday where Scripture does not command Sunday as the new day of worship, ) s
5 93 M
(then the real question becomes whose authority he is accepting. In that framework the mark of ) s
5 80 M
(the beast is bound up with accepting human religious authority over God's expressed will.) s
5 54 M
(They also set the mark over against God's sign. Quoting a statement that cites Exodus 31:13, ) s
5 41 M
(they identify the Sabbath as God's sign or seal, because it marks Him as Creator and Sanctifier. ) s
5 28 M
(In that contrast, the mark of the beast is the rival sign of rival authority. So the final issue is not ) s
5 15 M
(technology as such. It is worship, obedience, and whether one receives God's sign or the sign of ) s
5 2 M
(a power that claims the right to alter God's law.) s
