(The principle is plain across Scripture. The Spirit is the Spirit of truth. Christ is the truth. ) s
5 223 M
(Nathanael is commended because there was no guile in him. Second Thessalonians says the lost ) s
5 210 M
(perish because they did not receive the love of the truth. No deviation from strict integrity ) s
5 197 M
(meets God's approval. Even under real pressure, the right move is honesty: when the Gestapo ) s
5 184 M
(came to Corrie ten Boom's house looking for a man she was hiding under a tablecloth, she told ) s
5 171 M
(them he was right under the table, and they laughed it off and left. God is able to defend. He ) s
5 158 M
(does not need us to take things into our own hands.) s
5 132 M
(Situation ethics \342\\200\\224 the idea that love sometimes requires you to lie, or even to commit ) s
5 119 M
(adultery, to secure a loving outcome \342\\200\\224 replaces God's law with the inclinations of the ) s
5 106 M
(heart, and Jeremiah 17 warns that the heart is deceitful above all things and only the Lord truly ) s
5 93 M
(knows it.) s
5 67 M
(Examine the motive here. If the elder has stopped responding, a fake name will not produce a ) s
5 54 M
(godly conversation; it will produce another round of the same dispute under a mask. Pray. Let ) s
5 41 M
(God work on the person. Consider whether your own approach needs more humility and love. ) s
5 28 M
(If the Spirit is leading, He will open the door honestly. Deception is not that door.) s
5 2 M
(How should someone transition to keeping the Sabbath after discovering the truth, without ) s
