5 704 M
(simply turning his back on his former church?) s
5 678 M
(If you have become convinced from Scripture that the Sabbath is truth, then honor that truth ) s
5 665 M
(fully. Do not try to keep one foot in obedience and one foot in a church system that rejects the ) s
5 652 M
(light God has shown you.) s
5 626 M
(Once you decide to follow the Bible, other decisions follow. The real issue is not whether you ) s
5 613 M
(feel attached to your former church. The real issue is whether the Word of God is supreme, or ) s
5 600 M
(whether church loyalty is supreme. If your church does not teach the whole truth, then sooner ) s
5 587 M
(or later you have to decide whether you will accommodate error or obey God.) s
5 561 M
(Matthew 6:24 makes the point plainly: you cannot serve two masters. Once truth is understood, ) s
5 548 M
(truth calls for obedience, not partial commitment. The Sabbath is not treated as a minor point ) s
5 535 M
(either. Ezekiel 20:12 is used to show that God gave the Sabbath as a sign between Himself and ) s
5 522 M
(His people, so keeping it is part of accepting His rulership and sanctifying work in your life.) s
5 496 M
(So the transition should be real. You need to plant yourself where the truth is taught, not ) s
5 483 M
(remain settled in a body that rejects what God has shown you. This may mean severing ties ) s
5 470 M
(with a church as an institution.) s
5 444 M
(But that does not mean severing ties with people. Keep the friendships. Cherish them. Use your ) s
5 431 M
(influence with love and patience. Stay in contact and witness to them. Share the light you have ) s
5 418 M
(found. The point is not to abandon people. The point is to stop participating in a system that ) s
5 405 M
(continues in error while still trying to help the people inside it.) s
5 379 M
(Do not try to live in both worlds at once. You cannot keep Sabbath privately, then continue in a ) s
5 366 M
(Sunday church as though the doctrinal divide does not matter. Sooner or later a choice has to be ) s
5 353 M
(made. Coming to Christ means turning your back on error, not merely adding one more truth ) s
5 340 M
(to an otherwise unchanged life.) s
5 314 M
(So transition with love, but transition decisively. Obey God rather than men. Leave partial truth ) s
5 301 M
(behind. Keep your relationships open for witness, but do not treat membership in error as if it ) s
5 288 M
(were spiritually neutral.) s
5 262 M
(How should Christians practice tithing today, especially with fixed salaries, gross-versus-net ) s
5 249 M
(questions, financial strain, and concerns about how leaders use the money?) s
5 223 M
(Treat tithing as a faith issue before you treat it as an accounting puzzle.) s
5 197 M
(Tithe is not presented mainly as a financial technique but as an act of trust. If you only pay tithe ) s
5 184 M
(when the numbers already feel comfortable, then the whole faith element disappears. Tithing is ) s
5 171 M
(meant to say, Lord, what I have has come from You, and I trust You enough to return what You ) s
5 158 M
(claim as Yours.) s
5 132 M
(On that basis, reject the idea that a salaried person should tithe only on the raise or only on ) s
5 119 M
(occasional increase beyond regular wages. Each paycheck is increase when you receive it. So the ) s
5 106 M
(tenth is taken from the salary itself, not merely from some later bump above your normal ) s
5 93 M
(earnings.) s
5 67 M
(Return tithe on the gross, not on what remains after taxes, bills, and deductions. If you wait ) s
5 54 M
(until everything else is paid first, then God is being treated as the leftover claimant instead of ) s
5 41 M
(the first claimant. The reasoning is simple: the tithe belongs to God before you start arranging ) s
5 28 M
(the rest of your spending.) s
5 2 M
(Hard circumstances do not remove the principle. In fact, the very pressure of limited income is ) s
