(Does 1 Corinthians 7:14 \342\\200\\224 that the children of a mixed marriage "would be unclean, ) s
5 535 M
(but now they are holy" \342\\200\\224 mean children are born with a sinful nature?) s
5 509 M
(No, this is not a text about a child's nature at birth. It is about the home.) s
5 483 M
(Paul is addressing a couple who were both unbelievers when they married and then one spouse ) s
5 470 M
(came to faith. He is not addressing the question of whether to enter an unequally yoked ) s
5 457 M
(marriage. His point is that the believing spouse should not automatically divorce. The believing ) s
5 444 M
(spouse does not become defiled by the unbelieving one; the opposite moves in. The unbelieving ) s
5 431 M
(spouse is sanctified by the believing one, and that holy influence spills over onto the children, ) s
5 418 M
(so that they are called holy rather than unclean. If the marriage were torn up, that sanctifying ) s
5 405 M
(influence on the home and on the children would be lost.) s
5 379 M
(So "unclean" and "holy" here describe standing inside the covenant household under the ) s
5 366 M
(influence of a believing parent, not the ontological condition of the child. The passage is not ) s
5 353 M
(saying anything about sinful nature in either direction.) s
5 327 M
(How does the seventh commandment apply to angels and other non-human beings who do not ) s
5 314 M
(marry? And why do animals procreate if they are not repopulating heaven?) s
5 288 M
(The ten commandments are eternal in principle and adapted in expression. The fourth ) s
5 275 M
(commandment, for example, mentions the manservant and maidservant \342\\200\\224 that is a ) s
5 262 M
(human application of an eternal principle. The seventh commandment works the same way.) s
5 236 M
(At the principle level, adultery and fornication are disloyalty. A pure woman in Scripture ) s
5 223 M
(stands for a faithful church; a harlot stands for a church that has abandoned Christ and joined ) s
5 210 M
(herself to the kings of the earth. Revelation's harlot committing fornication with the kings is ) s
5 197 M
(that union of church and state \342\\200\\224 and it is a violation of the seventh commandment in ) s
5 184 M
(principle. Paul uses the same logic when he tells believers not to be unequally yoked with ) s
5 171 M
(unbelievers. Lucifer is the original fornicator in that sense: he forsook Christ and fell in love ) s
5 158 M
(with himself, coveted a position that was not his, and in principle broke every one of the ten ) s
5 145 M
(commandments. So the seventh commandment applies to every moral being in the universe. It ) s
5 132 M
(governs loyalty, not only human sexuality.) s
5 106 M
(On animals: they procreate because the ecosystem of this world requires it. God created animals ) s
5 93 M
(for the life of the earth, foresaw sin and death entering, and gave them the capacity to replenish ) s
5 80 M
(so that the order of nature would continue. Genesis 1:28, where God tells the humans to be ) s
5 67 M
(fruitful and multiply and have dominion, sets up the human-animal relationship as ) s
5 54 M
(stewardship, not exploitation. Animals multiply to serve nature's balance and to serve ) s
5 41 M
(humanity's life on earth. That is the purpose; repopulating heaven is not.) s
5 15 M
