5 171 M
(in 2 Kings 3?) s
5 145 M
(God does not destroy a nation arbitrarily. He destroys it when it has gone beyond the point of ) s
5 132 M
(no return, and only He knows when that line is crossed.) s
5 106 M
(Genesis 15 sets the pattern. God promised Abraham the land but delayed its possession by four ) s
5 93 M
(hundred years "because the iniquity of the Amorite is not yet full." Probation, in effect, had not ) s
5 80 M
(closed on them. By the time of Moses, several generations later, that fullness had been reached. ) s
