(Christians can freely navigate to maintain order in society, which is the principle drawn from 1 ) s
5 691 M
(Peter 2.) s
5 665 M
(While the names of the days may have pagan origins and the secular world operates from ) s
5 652 M
(midnight to midnight, the actual seven-day sequential cycle established at creation remains ) s
5 639 M
(completely unbroken. Historical calendar adjustments, such as the shift from the Julian to the ) s
5 626 M
(Gregorian calendar in 1582, changed the dates to correct astronomical drift but never ) s
5 613 M
(interrupted the continuous cycle of the week itself.) s
5 587 M
(Therefore, you do not need to superimpose biblical timekeeping onto secular interactions. You ) s
5 574 M
(have discretion over how you manage the six working days. The only requirement is to render ) s
