5 587 M
(system for debt relief. Even when foreigners became permanent servants \(like the Gibeonites ) s
5 574 M
(who tricked Joshua\), they were not abused. They lived with their families, possessed land, and ) s
5 561 M
(were grafted into Israel. ) s
5 535 M
(God's laws heavily regulated the practice to protect human dignity. Slaves were explicitly ) s
5 522 M
(granted Sabbath rest and could not be worked seven days a week. Furthermore, Deuteronomy ) s
5 509 M
(23 explicitly commanded that if a slave escaped from an abusive master, they were not to be ) s
5 496 M
(returned\342\\200\\224a law that completely contradicts modern fugitive slave laws. While the ) s
5 483 M
(system allowed for foreign servitude, it strictly forbade cruelty, exploitation, and ruling over ) s
5 470 M
(anyone with "rigor.") s
