(scene.) s
5 379 M
(Are church manuals and books of order replacing the Bible? Are we in danger of putting more ) s
5 366 M
(authority in them than the Bible, hindering the Protestant principle of Scripture alone by ) s
5 353 M
(teaching the commandments of men \(Matthew 15:3-9\)?) s
5 327 M
(The Seventh-day Adventist Church maintains the firm Protestant position of the Bible and the ) s
5 314 M
(Bible alone as its supreme authority. The Church Manual and other policy books do not replace, ) s
5 301 M
(contradict, or supersede Scripture. They are only legitimate insofar as they harmonize with the ) s
5 288 M
(Word of God.) s
5 262 M
(The purpose of the Church Manual is not to establish new doctrines, but to serve as an ) s
5 249 M
(operational guide to maintain order, protect sound doctrine, prevent the abuse of authority, and ) s
5 236 M
(promote global unity. It provides the practical "nuts and bolts" for how the church ) s
5 223 M
(operates\342\\200\\224defining the roles of pastors, elders, and deacons, outlining how to conduct ) s
5 210 M
(elections and ceremonies, and explaining how to handle church discipline biblically. ) s
5 184 M
(There is a clear distinction between the Bible and these manuals. The Church Manual can only ) s
5 171 M
(be amended by a vote of the full global delegation at a General Conference Session, ensuring ) s
5 158 M
(broad consensus rather than arbitrary top-down decrees. There are also working policies for ) s
5 145 M
(day-to-day administration \(like salaries and properties\) and a Minister's Manual for conducting ) s
5 132 M
(ceremonies. Problems only arise when these manuals are applied unevenly\342\\200\\224such as ) s
5 119 M
(when local conferences ignore global policies or invent rules to ban speakers improperly. When ) s
5 106 M
(applied correctly and kept subordinate to the Bible, the manuals are a necessary blessing that ) s
5 93 M
(keeps a global movement united and functioning smoothly.) s
5 67 M
